      "id": "vsl_cursor_record",
      "rule": "vsl.h VSL_Next: vsl_more means \"Cursor points to next log record\"; VSL_Check, VSL_Match, VSL_Print, VSL_PrintTerse and VSL_Write read c->rec. After end, EOF or an error the mmap cursor's rec is at or past the end of the mapping (vsl_cursor.c vslc_mmap_next), so a record is read only after VSL_Next returned vsl_more (ok:VSL_Next). VSL_ResetCursor, VSL_PrintAll, VSL_WriteAll and the transaction printers move the cursor on (to its end); a new cursor has no record yet.",
